        "answer": {
          "short": "$P(B\\mid A)=P(B)$, by substituting $P(A\\mid B)=P(A)$ in the result from part (a).",
          "worked": "Since $A$ is independent of $B$, $P(A\\mid B)=P(A)$. Using the ratio in part (a),\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(B\\mid A)&=\\frac{P(B)}{P(A)}\\times P(A\\mid B)\\\\P(B\\mid A)&=\\frac{P(B)}{P(A)}\\times P(A)\\\\P(B\\mid A)&=P(B).\\end{align*}$$",
